From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: no "Contact Google Disability Support" in
 Accessibility

Settings > Accessibility ended with "Contact Google Disability Support",
a link to Google's help center, where Google's support team helps people
with ChromeOS on Chromebooks. NickelOS isn't Google's to support, so the
row is gone.

---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_a11y_page/os_a11y_page.html b/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_a11y_page/os_a11y_page.html
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_a11y_page/os_a11y_page.html
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_a11y_page/os_a11y_page.html
@@ -77,13 +77,8 @@
             external>
         </cr-link-row>
       </template>
-      <cr-link-row
-          id="disabilitySupportLink" class="hr"
-          start-icon="os-settings:a11y-contact-support"
-          label="$i18n{disabilitySupportTitle}"
-          on-click="onDisabilitySupportClick_"
-          external>
-      </cr-link-row>
+      <!-- NickelOS: no "Contact Google Disability Support" (Google's help
+           center, for ChromeOS on Chromebooks). -->
     </settings-card>
   </div>
 
